<concept id="t00297">
	<title>Operating high beam</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>lighting 
					<indexterm>operating high beam</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>operating high beam</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02265">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e02266">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OSW035464L.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e02267"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ul id="e02268">
			<li>
				<p>To turn on the high beams, push the lever away from you.</p>
				<p>The lever will return to its original position, and the high beam indicator (<image href="../../images/WKIA_046.eps" align="left" scale="15" placement="inline" outputclass="nolabel" id="e02269"/>) will illuminate on the instrument cluster.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>To flash the headlights, pull the lever toward you and then release it.</p>
				<p>The lever will return to the normal (low beam) position.</p>
				<p>The headlight switch does not need to be <term translate="no">ON</term> to use the flash feature.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<note type="warning" id="e02270">
			<p>Do not use the high beams when other vehicles are nearby, as this may obstruct other drivers’ vision.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
</concept>